# The biggest product-level problem: none of the supplier integrations are actually live

`LCSCAdapter` says:

```python
if not self.api_key:
    fixture

# Would call LCSC API here
# For MVP, use seed fixtures
return fixture
```

Even **with an API key**, it still returns fixtures.

M5Stack and Waveshare are fixtures too.

So we currently have:

> resolver over hand-entered demo data

not:

> normalized supplier API.

That's okay for the first commit, but don't call this checkpoint complete.

The next checkpoint needs at least **one genuinely live supplier**.

I would make that LCSC or whichever official endpoint can be authenticated quickest.

The adapter contract needs:

```text
mode:
live
fixture
cached
```

and every returned result needs:

```text
source_mode
observed_at
raw_hash
```

Never make fixture data look live.

