# The current tests are mostly theater

Not useless — but they prove too little.

For example:

```python
test_desk_head
```

only checks:

```python
status == resolved
len(routes) > 0
cost <= 50
```

It does **not** prove:

```text
all requested capabilities are satisfied
exactly two axes exist
Wi-Fi exists if required
parts connect together
supplier SKUs exist
evidence exists
route is genuinely orderable
```

Likewise `test_plant_node` doesn't even assert that soil moisture was satisfied — and there isn't an obvious soil moisture fixture in the adapters I inspected.

So the system may say `"resolved"` while failing the request.

Replace benchmark tests with hard invariants:

```python
assert set(requested_caps) <= set(route["capabilities_satisfied"])
assert route["capabilities_missing"] == []
assert route["estimated_parts_cost_usd"] <= budget
assert all(part["supplier_sku"] for part in route["parts"])
assert all(part["source_url"] for part in route["parts"])
```

And importantly:

```python
assert no_hard_compatibility_failures(route)
```

